<title>FRANCE: Jospin to question French private pensions laws.</title>
<headline>Jospin to question French private pensions laws.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Socialist Prime Minister Lionel Jospin told parliament on Thursday that pension reforms introduced by the former centre-right government could hurt the current state-backed system and would be called into question.</p>
<p>&quot;The measures recently adopted on (private) pension funds, which could do damage to the shared retirement benefit regime, will be called into question,&quot; he said in a kenote policy speech.</p>
<p>The outgoing government proposed a bill introducing private pension funds in France which was adopted earlier this year but has yet to be put into force.</p>
</text>
